@* Cover image layered over a placeholder that shows through whenever the image
   is absent OR fails to load - a cover missing from the public R2 bucket, or an
   offline device. Without the failure case the browser paints its own broken-image
   glyph (the grey question mark on iOS Safari), which reads as the app being broken.

   onerror is an inline attribute, not @@onerror: the DOM error event doesn't bubble,
   so Blazor's delegated root listener never sees it. Hiding rather than removing the
   <img> keeps Blazor's diffing view of the DOM intact. *@

<div class="book-cover">
    <div class="cover-placeholder"><Icon Name="menu_book" Size="48" /></div>

    @if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(Url))
    {
        <img src="@Url"
             alt="Cover of @(Title ?? "this book")"
             loading="lazy"
             onerror="this.hidden = true" />
    }
</div>

@code {
    [Parameter] public string? Url { get; set; }
    [Parameter] public string? Title { get; set; }
}
